# {{.MemoryPluginName}}: your demarkus {{.Store}} is available

Your {{.Store}} is a versioned demarkus store behind the `{{.MemoryPluginName}}` MCP tools; "recall" and "record" here always mean it, never the host's built-in memory. Treat it like {{.RepoInstructions}}: consult before starting, record as you go, unprompted. {{if eq .Harness "claude"}}Never disable Claude Code's built-in memory tool unasked.{{else}}Never disable the host's built-in memory unasked.{{end}}

Everything lives under `/<slug>/`. Write through the bound store's tools ({{.ToolForm}}); the server's instructions carry the read contract. Ambiguous target: ask the user once.

## Recall first

Before "what do I know / did we decide / have we seen X" and at the start of substantive work, `mark_lookup` `/<slug>/` with descriptive subjects; `/<slug>/index.md` is the backstop for untagged content. Never fabricate recall.

## Record as you go

Write without prompting: decisions to `/<slug>/adr/<NNNN>-<title>.md`, bug lessons to `/<slug>/debugging.md`, patterns to `/<slug>/patterns.md`, session progress through `/soul-journal`, and architecture, roadmap, debt, plans or open questions to their file under `/<slug>/`. Keep `/<slug>/index.md` current. The `remember` skill has the layout. Write-time gates (tags, destination, retention, style) say what to fix; follow them.

## Restraint

No trivia, chat, secrets, or anything derivable from the repo and git history. Capture the non-obvious: why, patterns, gotchas. Shared or authoritative knowledge goes to a knowledge system through `/promote`, never a direct write. `/soul-context` primes a session, `/soul-journal` appends today's entry, `/soul-status` diagnoses the server.